@startuml seq-06-password-change
' ============================================================
' SEQ-06: POST /auth/change-password - current alpha implementation
' ============================================================

title SEQ-06: POST /auth/change-password - update hash and revoke refresh tokens

autonumber

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #2E7D32
  LifeLineBorderColor #1B5E20
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F5E9
  ParticipantBorderColor #1B5E20
  ActorBackgroundColor #FFEFCD
  ActorBorderColor #AA6622
  NoteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7
  NoteBorderColor #AA8800
}

actor "Dashboard" as Dashboard
participant "JwtBearer" as Bearer
participant "HttpActorContext" as Actor
participant "AuthEndpoints\nPOST /auth/change-password\n[RequireAuthorization]" as AE
participant "AuthService" as Auth
participant "IUserRepository" as Users
participant "IPasswordHasher" as Hasher
participant "IRefreshTokenRepository" as RT
database "controlit_users" as UDB
database "controlit_refresh_tokens" as RTDB

Dashboard -> Bearer: POST /auth/change-password\nAuthorization: Bearer <access>\n{ currentPassword, newPassword }
activate Bearer
Bearer -> Bearer: validate JWT\nissuer, audience, signature, lifetime
Bearer -> Actor: claims available\nsub, email, role, tenant_id?
Bearer -> AE: authenticated
deactivate Bearer
activate AE

AE -> Auth: ChangePasswordAsync(Actor.UserId, request)
activate Auth
Auth -> Users: GetByIdAsync(userId)
Users -> UDB: SELECT * FROM controlit_users WHERE id=@id
UDB --> Users: user | null
Users --> Auth

alt user missing
  Auth --> AE: KeyNotFoundException
  AE --> Dashboard: error middleware response
end

== Current password check ==

Auth -> Hasher: Verify(request.CurrentPassword, user.PasswordHash)
Hasher --> Auth: ok?

alt current password wrong
  Auth --> AE: UnauthorizedAccessException\n"Current password is incorrect."
  AE --> Dashboard: 401 Problem
end

== Password policy ==

Auth -> Auth: EnforcePasswordPolicy(newPassword)\nlength >= 12\nat least 3 of upper/lower/digit/symbol

alt policy fails
  Auth --> AE: InvalidOperationException
  AE --> Dashboard: 400 Problem\npolicy message
end

Auth -> Hasher: Verify(newPassword, currentHash)
Hasher --> Auth: same?

alt new password equals current
  Auth --> AE: InvalidOperationException\n"New password must differ..."
  AE --> Dashboard: 400 Problem
end

== Persist and revoke refresh tokens ==

Auth -> Hasher: Hash(newPassword)
Hasher --> Auth: newHash
Auth -> Users: UpdateAsync(user)\nPasswordHash=newHash\nPasswordChangedAt=now\nMustChangePassword=false
Users -> UDB: UPDATE controlit_users
UDB --> Users

Auth -> RT: RevokeAllForUserAsync(userId)
RT -> RTDB: UPDATE controlit_refresh_tokens\nSET revoked_at=now\nWHERE user_id=@uid AND revoked_at IS NULL
RTDB --> RT

Auth --> AE: success
deactivate Auth
AE --> Dashboard: 204 No Content
deactivate AE

note right of Dashboard
  Current code does not clear refresh cookie in this endpoint.
  Because all refresh rows are revoked, next /auth/refresh fails.
  Current frontend shows success and keeps in-memory access token
  until expiry or another auth transition.
end note

note bottom of Auth
  Access token remains valid until normal JWT expiry (900s).
  Refresh-based continuation is blocked by revoked refresh rows.
end note

@enduml
